' What a closed player may still do. Once the viewer has left (Back, a remote
' Stop, a deep link or reminder taking over), the screen is popped but its
' observers live on until MainScene reaps its API task, and anything still in
' flight lands on them: a stream answer, a channel roll-over's next item. Each
' of those used to start the Video node again off-screen, so audio played
' after the viewer left and the server saw a play session start that nothing
' would ever stop (Roku side of sashimi-apple#886). Pure, so
' tests/PlayerSessionTests.brs can run it off-device; PlayerScreen applies it.
namespace PlayerSession

    ' Whether an API answer is still acted on after the player has closed.
    ' Only the watch-state writes are: their answers tell the screen
    ' underneath to re-read its episodes. Everything else would start,
    ' restart or extend playback that is over.
    function actsAfterClose(action as dynamic) as boolean
        if type(action) <> "String" and type(action) <> "roString" then return false
        return action = "reportStopped" or action = "markPlayed"
    end function

end namespace
